<%# Faithful port of the legacy SPA `Hujah/card_header.js`: avatar + full_name + @handle,
    plus a share menu (native <details>, no JS needed). Optional `parent:` local
    renders the "Response to ..." parent stub (port of card_parent.js).

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.3) —
    docs/design-system/components/hujah/HujahHeader.prompt.md: "full name is indigo
    medium; `@handle · date` is 14px grey underneath. Timestamps are always the compact
    `%b %-d` form." The name and the timestamp format were already right; the 14px was
    not. A bare `<small>` is 0.8em, i.e. 12.8px against the body's 16px — the design
    system's UI text is 14px, so both `<small>`s here now say `text-sm` outright. Same
    correction, same reason, as the navbar labels in Task 4.1: they were inheriting a
    size rather than being assigned one.

    Both avatars go through `ui/_avatar` — 44px (`md`) for the byline, 32px (`sm`) for
    the parent stub, which are the design system's own boxes for those two slots. That
    is not only tidiness: `image_tag user.photo` RAISES when `photo` is blank, and
    `:photo` is user-editable while `assign_random_photo` only backfills on create. This
    partial renders inside every feed card, so one photoless author 500s the whole feed.
    Pass the box through `size:`, never a `w-*` in `class:` — those compete rather than
    override, and the bundle's order decides (see the partial's own header).

    The stub's `shadow-sm` stays. It is the only `shadow-sm` in the app and it is NOT
    the card shadow: this strip sits above the byline inside a card that already has
    `shadow`, and promoting it to a full `shadow` would read as a second card edge —
    which is precisely what ui/_divider's header says internal sections must not grow. %>
<% if local_assigns[:parent].present? %>
  <%= link_to hujah_path(parent.slug), class: "block no-underline" do %>
    <div class="shadow-sm border-b border-light-grey px-4 py-1 flex items-center">
      <%= render "ui/avatar", user: parent.user, size: :sm, class: "mr-2" %>
      <div class="flex flex-col min-w-0">
        <small class="text-sm text-grey">
          Response to <span class="text-primary"><%= parent.user.full_name %></span>'s hoojah
        </small>
        <div class="text-grey text-sm truncate max-w-[350px]"><%= strip_tags(parent.body) %></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  <% end %>
<% end %>

<div class="px-4 pt-3 pb-0 flex justify-between items-center">
  <div class="flex items-center min-w-0">
    <%= link_to "#", class: "shrink-0" do %>
      <%= render "ui/avatar", user: hujah.user, size: :md, class: "mr-3" %>
    <% end %>
    <div class="flex flex-col min-w-0">
      <%= link_to hujah.user.full_name, "#", class: "text-primary font-medium no-underline truncate" %>
      <small class="text-sm text-grey">
        @<%= hujah.user.username %>
        <span class="mx-1">·</span>
        <%# `data-local="time-ago"` is local_time's hook — the compact "%b %-d" here is
            the server-rendered fallback the design system specifies, not a placeholder. %>
        <time datetime="<%= hujah.created_at.iso8601 %>" data-local="time-ago"><%= hujah.created_at.strftime("%b %-d") %></time>
      </small>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%= render "hujahs/share_menu", hujah: hujah %>
</div>
